\section{Overview}

The Berzerk sound hardware has two independent subsystems:

\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{S14001A speech synthesis chip}: plays digitized speech from a
  4~KB voice ROM.  Controlled via I/O port 0x44 (data/control write, busy
  read).
\item \textbf{Exidy custom sound board}: a Motorola 6840 Programmable Timer
  Module driving a noise/tone generator circuit.  Accessed via I/O ports
  0x40--0x43, 0x45, 0x47 (timer registers) and 0x46 (SFX control latch).
\end{itemize}

This module provides \textbf{stub implementations} for Phase 4.  The I/O
register behavior is correct enough that the game code will not hang on
polling loops (the S14001A busy flag clears immediately, the 6840 registers
accept reads and writes).  No actual audio generation occurs.  Real audio
will be added in a later phase.

