\section{Data Structures}

\subsection{S14001A Speech Chip State}

The S14001A has a busy flag, the current word address being spoken, a
volume setting, and a clock divisor.  For the stub, we only need [[busy]]
to satisfy the game's polling loop and the register values for
observability.

<<s14001a state struct>>=
struct S14001AState {
    bool busy = false;
    uint8_t word_addr = 0;     // 6-bit word address (0-63)
    uint8_t volume = 0;        // 3-bit volume (0-7)
    uint8_t clock_div = 16;    // divisor (16 - (control & 7))
};
@

\subsection{Exidy 6840 Timer State}

The 6840 has 8 registers (3 timers with control, count, and latch registers
plus a status register).  The SFX control latch selects the sound effect.
For the stub we store the register file and the latch value.

<<exidy 6840 state struct>>=
struct Exidy6840State {
    std::array<uint8_t, 8> regs;
    uint8_t sfx_latch = 0;

    Exidy6840State() {
        regs.fill(0);
    }
};
@

\subsection{Combined Sound State}

<<sound state struct>>=
struct SoundState {
    S14001AState speech;
    Exidy6840State timer;
    const uint8_t* voice_rom = nullptr;
    uint32_t voice_rom_size = 0;
};
@

